Cell["\<\
generates the standard topology file that includes {\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NF\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]} \
and {{6, 7, 8}, {5, 8, 9}, {4, 9, 10}, {1, 10, 11}, {2, 3, 11}}. 
The reverse is true as well: the graph can be constructed from the \
information in {\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NF\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]} and {{6, 7, 8}, {5, 8, 9}, \
{4, 9, 10}, {1, 10, 11}, {2, 3, 11}}, which makes for a more compact topology \
definition that is also not reliant on Mathematica. We provide topologies in \
that format in \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]topology text files\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], which also define the topology names, e.g. \
dim7-4F-1S.dat contains
T[7][1]\t{\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]}\t\
{{2, 3, 6}, {1, 6, 7}, {4, 5, 7}}
T[7][2]\t{\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]S\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]F\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NF\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]}\t\
{{1, 3, 6}, {2, 6, 7}, {4, 5, 7}}
which defines the name T[operator mass dimension d][topology] and the \
topology structure.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9678385547688437`*^9, 3.96783877572106*^9}, {
  3.967838888590053*^9, 3.967838902146833*^9}, {3.969100076247036*^9, 
  3.969100246000931*^9}, {3.970582893568584*^9, 
  3.9705829029322567`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d4fed08e-596d-4d9d-a7c8-\
b0013bf0deb4"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Side note: directed graphs and momentum flow", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96910025960122*^9, 3.969100279150443*^9}, {
  3.969363351492187*^9, 3.969363358643927*^9}, {3.970583767005835*^9, 
  3.970583769716482*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8ce8241e-aaa2-4f2d-99ed-\
fc165224e0d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The third entry in our topology files, e.g.  {{6, 7, 8}, {5, 8, 9}, {4, 9, \
10}, {1, 10, 11}, {2, 3, 11}}, defines the charge or momentum flow through \
our diagram. We treat all external particles as incoming, and internal \
particles flow from the first vertex they appear in to the second. So in this \
example, the internal particle 8 goes from the vertex {6, 7, 8} to {5, 8, 9}, \
i.e. it is outgoing at the first vertex and incoming at the second. We can \
show this explicitly in the graph using arrows or directed edges. \n\nThe \
code below provides the function MomentumGraph, which takes a graph like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  GraphicsBox[
   NamespaceBox["NetworkGraphics",
    DynamicModuleBox[{Typeset`graph = HoldComplete[
      Graph[{
       "Vertex[1][8]", "Vertex[3][7]", "Vertex[1][11]", "Vertex[3][11]", 
        "Vertex[1][12]", "Vertex[1][4]", "Vertex[3][5]", "Vertex[1][6]", 
        "Vertex[3][6]", "Vertex[1][9]", "Vertex[3][9]", "Vertex[1][10]"}, {
       Null, {{1, 2}, {3, 4}, {5, 4}, {6, 7}, {8, 9}, {10, 11}, {12, 11}, {9, 
        7}, {9, 11}, {2, 7}, {2, 4}}}, {
       EdgeLabels -> {UndirectedEdge["Vertex[1][4]", "Vertex[3][5]"] -> Placed[
            Text["4", Background -> GrayLevel[1]], {Left, "Middle"}], 
          UndirectedEdge["Vertex[1][8]", "Vertex[3][7]"] -> Placed[
            Text["1", Background -> GrayLevel[1]], {Left, "Middle"}], 
          UndirectedEdge["Vertex[1][10]", "Vertex[3][9]"] -> Placed[
            Text["7", Background -> GrayLevel[1]], {Left, "Middle"}], 
